 know try to flesh out  ahead of time what the implications of  some things these things could be and  personally I'd be all in favor of  disconnecting the the need to earn a  living from the way we choose to spend  our time during the day yeah and it I  mean really it is about breaking that  link that's what is going to be with  what's valuable to us and the other  thing I would say as well just on a  final note is that this notion of  sketching lots of different scenarios  and plans I mean that I would view that  as being the main thing that I do which  is that I try to imagine different  possible futures and evaluate them using  different kind of ethical norms and  principles so that we get a sense of the  broadness of the axial article landscape  into which we are navigating today  define the word XE illogical I know what  it means but it's axiology is the study  of values so the different kinds of  values associated with these matters  right I find myself at the end of many  of my podcast interviews saying well  it's a brave new world things are gonna  be changing a lot and I think this is  definitely an example of that so John  Danner thanks so much for your insights  here this is a fun conversation yeah  thanks a lot Sean it's great
 

